docs {
  # mhAPI — inspect the metahub-api JSON endpoints used by metahub-ui.

  These requests target the `/api/v1/*` surface that the React UI
  consumes (collections, profiles, oras, version, session, registry
  tokens). They are distinct from the `/v2/*` OCI registry surface
  exercised by the qnib-ftest folder.

  ## Auth model

  metahub-api has TWO independent tokens:

    - `oci_bearer` — OCI Bearer for `/v2/*` (minted via the
      WWW-Authenticate challenge in qnib-ftest/refreshToken).
    - `mhapi_jwt`  — metahub-api JWT for `/api/v1/protected/*`
      (minted via `godmodeLogin` below).

  This folder defaults to `auth: bearer` carrying `{{mhapi_jwt}}`.
  Public endpoints (`/api/v1/collections`, `/api/v1/profiles`, etc.)
  ignore the header; protected endpoints (`/api/v1/protected/*`)
  require it.

  ## Sequence

  Run in order — public calls work without auth, protected calls
  require `godmodeLogin` to have populated `mhapi_jwt`.

    0. godmodeLogin        — POST /api/v1/godmode/login,
                             stores `mhapi_jwt` in active env
                             (mirrors UI godmodeLogin() in
                             metahub-ui/src/lib/api.ts).
    1. getAuthConfig       — GET /api/v1/auth/config — discover
                             whether oidc / godmode are enabled.
                             Used by the UI's Login page to pick
                             which flow to render.
    2. getVersion          — GET /api/v1/version — api + metalib
                             versions baked into the running binary.
                             Surfaced in the UI footer; also drives
                             the GoCD verify-ce deploy guard.
    3. listProfiles        — GET /api/v1/profiles — profile catalog
                             used by `<ProfileSelector>`. Extracts
                             the first profile's `label` into
                             `mhapi_profile_label` for step 4.
    4. getProfileDetail    — GET /api/v1/profiles/{label} — full
                             profile incl. manipulations. Powers
                             the Profile detail page and its
                             ManipulationCard sections.
    5. listCollections     — POST /api/v1/collections with
                             `{repo}` body — collection list with
                             optional `profile` filter (used by
                             the Collections page). Extracts the
                             first collection's repo_name + first
                             tag's tag_name into
                             `mhapi_repo_name` / `mhapi_tag_name`
                             for step 6.
    6. getCollection       — POST /api/v1/collection with
                             `{repo_name, tag_name}` body — leaf
                             detail with manifests, layers, cpu_target
                             (post-surface-cpu-target-ui).
    7. listOras            — GET /api/v1/oras?repo=… — ORAS
                             artifact list for the OrasArtifacts page.
    8. getOrasArtifact     — GET /api/v1/oras/artifact?repo=…&artifact_type=…
                             — single artifact detail.
    9. getSession          — GET /api/v1/protected/session — current
                             user (requires `mhapi_jwt`).
   10. listRegistryTokens  — GET /api/v1/protected/registry-tokens
                             — Authentik app passwords for the
                             Settings page (requires `mhapi_jwt`).

  ## Variables

  Reads from the active environment:
    - `registry`  — metahub-api base URL (same host as /v2/*).
    - `username`, `password` — god-mode credentials (`oci` / `oci`
      in dev).
    - `repo`      — repo prefix to filter collections (`qnib/ftest`).
    - `oras_repo`, `oras_artifact_type` — for ORAS calls.

  Writes to the active environment:
    - `mhapi_jwt`              — metahub-api Bearer (step 0).
    - `mhapi_profile_label`    — first profile label (step 3).
    - `mhapi_repo_name`, `mhapi_tag_name` — collection coordinates
                                 (step 5).
}
